{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted","id":1394539,"title":"Do Fireworks exsist in Exalted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-06T04:49:24-07:00","id":1394539,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon7.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Do Fireworks exsist in Exalted?","content":"I think I understand how Fire Dust does not clearly equal Gunpowder (Fire Dust =/= Gunpowder).<br /> <br /> So it's not a given they could or would make Fireworks (or <u>Flares</u>, etc.), unless the ST allows it or there are examples of it in the books.<br /> <br /> Has there been any cannon account of Fireworks used in the setting I have failed to notice/remember?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media.gettyimages.com/photos/firework-rockets-picture-id493766000?b=1&amp;k=6&amp;m=493766000&amp;s=612x612&amp;w=0&amp;h=kHqtYIto6rgAms1hmQQteZADXctdX6c6S0KKUki4-J4=\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 06-06-2020, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T06:19:53-07:00","id":1394550,"title":"","content":"They definitely exist, albeit not sure how they're made beyond 'alchemy'...<br /> <br /> From page 24 of <i>The Realm</i>:<br /> <br /> <i>HOLIDAYS AND FESTIVALS<br /> The Realm observes numerous state holidays created by Imperial decree, religious festivals ordained by the Immaculate Order\u2019s prayer calendar, and traditional celebrations. The Day of Her Ascent celebrates the Empress\u2019 formal coronation, marked by lavish feasts and recitals of patriotic poetry and song. The Celebration of Seven Shattered Helms honors the Imperial legions, whose most distinguished troops once paraded before the Empress on that day to receive her commendation.<br /> <br /> The five days of Calibration at year\u2019s end are marked with drunken revelry and <u><b>alchemical fireworks</b></u>; Dynasts engage in absurd role reversals \u2014 satraps beg on street corners for coins, household heads kowtow to servants, and lucky peasants are made five-day queens.<br /> <br /> Other holidays are local and idiosyncratic. Pangu Prefecture commemorates the anniversary of the founder Cynis\u2019 Exaltation in a decadent festival funded by House Cynis. The peasants of Six Vines observe a holiday honoring the Hearth that slew a pack of hellboars threatening the town over a century ago. The Feast of Fallen Crusaders, a Shogunate- era holiday, is still celebrated in Lord\u2019s Crossing Dominion.</i><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> See also the pic on p.127 if you have the pdf.<br /> <br /> Hope that's some help at least...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 06-06-2020, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T07:19:29-07:00","id":1394554,"title":"","content":"Yes, but they must work differently enough from reality that the tech can\u2019t be weaponized for some reason. So we can assume the alchemical creation briefly becomes lighter than air before its eruption, rather than using combustion for lift, and then when it erupts it\u2019s just a burst of colored light with no destructive force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T16:46:31-07:00","id":1394659,"title":"","content":"I would think that fireworks <i>could</i> be weaponized, but because firedust and its analogues are extremely expensive, it's not cost effective to do so. Remember that IRL, black powder is cheap, but in Creation, its equivalent is <i>very</i> expensive outside of parts of the South. Even a small army is hideously costly, and enough<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huolongchushui\" target=\"_blank\"> fire dragons</a> to matter in a battle could quickly bankrupt all but the wealthiest states, and of course the Powers That Be are very much opposed to allowing mortals to mimic the abilities of the Dragon Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T21:39:48-07:00","id":1394720,"title":"","content":"The Dragon-Blood has a charm literally called Hopping Firecracker Evasion so firecracker is at least a thing in Creation, so firework also exist isn\u2019t so a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 06-07-2020, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:34:26-07:00","id":1394902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1394659#post1394659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that fireworks <i>could</i> be weaponized, but because firedust and its analogues are extremely expensive, it's not cost effective to do so. Remember that IRL, black powder is cheap, but in Creation, its equivalent is <i>very</i> expensive outside of parts of the South. Even a small army is hideously costly, and enough<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huolongchushui\" target=\"_blank\"> fire dragons</a> to matter in a battle could quickly bankrupt all but the wealthiest states, and of course the Powers That Be are very much opposed to allowing mortals to mimic the abilities of the Dragon Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>that would mean fireworks are only used as a conspicuous display of wealth though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:57:54-07:00","id":1394917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1394902#post1394902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that would mean fireworks are only used as a conspicuous display of wealth though</div> </div> </div> </div>This does not trouble me. Conspicuous displays of wealth are common throughout history and fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:00:36-07:00","id":1395278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1394720#post1394720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dragon-Blood has a charm literally called Hopping Firecracker Evasion so firecracker is at least a thing in Creation, so firework also exist isn\u2019t so a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Like Solar Charms (Exalted, pp. 250-251), Dragon-Blooded Charms aren\u2019t codified techniques or known entities within the setting of the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Charms are an abstraction, representing skill <br /> beyond mere mortal ken; though they\u2019re packaged and presented as individual rules and given memorable and evocative names for player convenience, in the world of Exalted Charms are more of a holistic mixture of personal prowess and the harnessing of Essence than a group of discrete techniques or \u201cpowers.\u201d Those who behold a Solar throwing aside a boulder would remark on her incredible strength, but not her use of Increasing Strength Exercise or Ten Ox Meditation.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Solar Charms aren\u2019t necessarily a known commodity in the world of Exalted. It may be that they don\u2019t exist. Each is a pretty package, depicting a magical feat which some Solar has been or will be capable of. But it is a feat belonging to that Solar\u2014the very Solar you create.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Simply put, we talk about Charms as power and magic and techniques, but it may be that the Solars are unaware of such codifications. When a player has her character use Monkey Leap Technique, the Solar leaps high into the air, high enough to clear a rooftop. It is easy to mistake the Charm for doing the work of hurling the Solar into the air, giving her magic legs or a boost of power, like a spell. But Charms aren\u2019t magic spells, and in the setting, the Solar is unaware of any such thing as Monkey Leap Technique. She has simply derived from her Athletics and her Solar Essence the power to leap very high and very far. It is through her prowess, excellence, and Essence that all Charms proceed. When we say things like \u201cThe magic of the Solars\u201d we are speaking to you, the reader, for your convenience.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The name of the Charm. Names only reflect our codification of the Solar Charm set and only in a few cases do they represent what the Exalted think their Charms are called.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think that holds Jen. But Moss Reynholm's reference is a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-09-2020, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T17:24:25-07:00","id":1395483,"title":"","content":"While true, charm names are somewhat illustrative of the game world even if the names aren't used in-character. We don't have charms with super anachronistic names like Soaring Jetfighter Spirit, Arrows Like Machinegun Bullets or Glorious Chainsaw Method- so the fact firecrackers are considered appropriate imagery does mean <i>something</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-09-2020, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T17:28:09-07:00","id":1395484,"title":"","content":"That's one of the biggest problems in Ex3: the developers take story and game separation to truly ludicrous levels. Characters don't know about Charms, they're not aware of their own Essence, there's no in-universe awareness of how the momentum of a fight is shifting (which is exactly what Initiative indicates), when a fighter is trying to force an opening for an effective strike and when he's aiming to exploit an opening (withering vs decisive attacks), and so on, which leads to severe logical problems. &quot;I extend my Essence into the great... &quot; &quot;NO! You don't know about Essence, you cannot consciously direct it, you cannot attune to the Artifact because there's no such thing as attunement! There are no Evocations! You have no magic powers and there are no magic &lt;whatever&gt;!&quot; &quot;So why do Artifacts get made?&quot; &quot;BECAUSE!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T17:37:48-07:00","id":1395486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1395484#post1395484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one of the biggest problems in Ex3: the developers take story and game separation to truly ludicrous levels. Characters don't know about Charms, they're not aware of their own Essence, there's no in-universe awareness of how the momentum of a fight is shifting (which is exactly what Initiative indicates), when a fighter is trying to force an opening for an effective strike and when he's aiming to exploit an opening (withering vs decisive attacks), and so on, which leads to severe logical problems. &quot;I extend my Essence into the great... &quot; &quot;NO! You don't know about Essence, you cannot consciously direct it, you cannot attune to the Artifact because there's no such thing as attunement! There are no Evocations! You have no magic powers and there are no magic &lt;whatever&gt;!&quot; &quot;So why do Artifacts get made?&quot; &quot;BECAUSE!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's overstating it really.<br /> TBH I think the sidebar was a bit heavy handed and that the advice should've been to hit people with the rulebook if they start navel gazing unironically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-09-2020, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T19:48:41-07:00","id":1395507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1395484#post1395484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one of the biggest problems in Ex3: the developers take story and game separation to truly ludicrous levels. Characters don't know about Charms, they're not aware of their own Essence, there's no in-universe awareness of how the momentum of a fight is shifting (which is exactly what Initiative indicates), when a fighter is trying to force an opening for an effective strike and when he's aiming to exploit an opening (withering vs decisive attacks), and so on, which leads to severe logical problems. &quot;I extend my Essence into the great... &quot; &quot;NO! You don't know about Essence, you cannot consciously direct it, you cannot attune to the Artifact because there's no such thing as attunement! There are no Evocations! You have no magic powers and there are no magic &lt;whatever&gt;!&quot; &quot;So why do Artifacts get made?&quot; &quot;BECAUSE!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm that's not what any of them say. The withering thing just says withering and decisive are abstraction, but the closest it goes to denying they exist is saying it wouldn't make sense for players to try harvesting eachother for momentum ie the twilight letting the dawn hit with them with withering to build up their momentum because withering attacks don't do damage and momentum doesn't care where it was generated.<br /> <br /> The charms not being things in universe is a bit weird, but considering the lexicon at the start of the core mentions charms are more of an instinctual and reflexive use of essence when compared to sorcery. I just figure it means that bit where charms were part of the exaltation to the point where Yozi automatically learned any new ones infernals made that lacked the heretical keyword isn't a thing.<br /> <br /> And I've never seen anything saying they don't know what essence is. You know with the entire DB finishing school dedicated to learning to use it, and essence fever being a thing and all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T19:57:59-07:00","id":1395511,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've always read it as just that, for example, Heaven Thunder Hammer isn't objectively in-universe called Heaven Thunder Hammer, it's just an abstraction of how some Solars can channel their Essence to make their strikes yeet a dude through walls. Any one Solar might decide to call that technique &quot;Heaven Thunder Hammer&quot; (hopefully with appropriate anime yelling), though. I've never read it, nor seen any indication that it was to be read, to such a degree that basic world elements connected to abstractions are wildly unknown by characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T08:01:40-07:00","id":1395597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1395483#post1395483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While true, charm names are somewhat illustrative of the game world even if the names aren't used in-character. We don't have charms with super anachronistic names like Soaring Jetfighter Spirit, Arrows Like Machinegun Bullets or Glorious Chainsaw Method- so the fact firecrackers are considered appropriate imagery does mean <i>something</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Equally, though, the Charm &quot;Cancel the Apocalypse&quot; is not proof that John of Patmos' Revelation writings exist in Creation.<br /> <br /> The Charm names aren't &quot;super anachronistic&quot; but they are explicitly addressed to the reader, not the character. I would be cautious about using them to infer details about the game world.<br /> <br /> &quot;What? Immaculate Golden Bow doesn't reveal me as an Anathema! It literally has Immaculate in the name!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T10:31:27-07:00","id":1395619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1395597#post1395597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Equally, though, the Charm &quot;Cancel the Apocalypse&quot; is not proof that John of Patmos' Revelation writings exist in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>nor the films of Guillermo del Toro.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Charm names aren't &quot;super anachronistic&quot; but they are explicitly addressed to the reader, not the character. I would be cautious about using them to infer details about the game world.<br /> <br /> &quot;What? Immaculate Golden Bow doesn't reveal me as an Anathema! It literally has Immaculate in the name!&quot; </div> </div> </div>I think one reasonable point of view is that the Charm names are what a character might call that power, if they happened to identify it as a specific technique. Like the Lunar Charm names use a lot of animal metaphors because Lunars would tend to describe their powers with animal metaphors if called upon to do so, even if Lunars from a particular part of Creation that have never seen that animal wouldn't use that specific one. I think it's reasonable to assume that all the animals mentioned in Lunar Charm titles exist in Creation for this reason.<br /> <br /> Like, one very clear influence on Exalted, and on the Charm names in particular, is martial arts and similar stories where people yell out the name of their technique before doing an attack. I'm very happy that the Exalted developers didn't want to make everyone into this type of character, or let someone who discovered a unique Charm following their personal journey run into someone who says &quot;oh, that's such-and-such technique&quot;. But it seems equally silly to me to say that these types of characters don't exist in exalted, or are limited to specifically yelling out the martial arts charm names, or to forbid people from shouting &quot;Monkey Leap Technique!&quot; when they jump 20 feet into the air. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T11:24:55-07:00","id":1395629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1395507#post1395507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Umm that's not what any of them say. The withering thing just says withering and decisive are abstraction, but the closest it goes to denying they exist is</div> </div> </div> </div>On page 190 to 191. It explicitly states, repeatedly and over the course of several paragraphs, that withering vs. Decisive is a purely out-if universe distinction, with every attack being intended to injure or kill, and Initiative solely a system abstraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T11:58:42-07:00","id":1395637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1395629#post1395629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> here's no in-universe awareness of how the momentum of a fight is shifting (which is exactly what Initiative indicates), when a fighter is trying to force an opening for an effective strike and when he's aiming to exploit an opening (withering vs decisive attacks)<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> On page 190 to 191. It explicitly states, repeatedly and over the course of several paragraphs, that withering vs. Decisive is a purely out-if universe distinction, with every attack being intended to injure or kill, and Initiative solely a system abstraction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you're reading too much into it. pp.190-191 also repeatedly and over the course of several paragraphs states that withering vs. decisive is meant to model cinematic combat. There is no such thing as cinematic combat where the combatants aren't aware of the momentum of combat, that's sort of the whole dramatic tension right there.<br /> <br /> Say a PC fights an enemy in heavy artifact armour. They are allowed to think this may be a problem and to decide they should weaken the armored foe first by going for the legs. The PC doesn't tell their allies &quot;Wait for my signal, I shall wither this foe so we can strike it decisively!&quot;, but they definitely recognize that they currently do not have the advantage in this fight and wish to turn that around.<br /> <br /> Same if someone gets crashed, this should very much be a dramatic moment which anyone present can recognize.<br /> <br /> &quot;Characters aren't aware of withering/decisive&quot; is more to prevent scenarios like a PC that says: &quot;We need more momentum to win this fight! <b>Just plink arrows or something, </b><b>it doesn't matter since we can't kill him yet!</b>&quot;. THAT is a system awareness that breaks versimilitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 06-10-2020, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T12:15:28-07:00","id":1395640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1395629#post1395629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On page 190 to 191. It explicitly states, repeatedly and over the course of several paragraphs, that withering vs. Decisive is a purely out-if universe distinction, with every attack being intended to injure or kill, and Initiative solely a system abstraction.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're kind of missing the part where it says that withering attacks should be labeled as serious attempts, but can also be described as feints or things intended to force an opening. What it explicitly says isn't acceptable is &quot;I wither him him to steal initiative.&quot;<br /> <br /> Feints, attempts at making openings, distractions, and all that are perfectly fine and there's nothing saying people don't know about them. Its that as Epitome says your character wouldn't be going &quot;Okay we need more initiative to overcome the enemies defenses, just keep withering until he's crashed that should give us enough momentum to do the job.&quot; It would be a plan to pin the enemy down to get a shot at a week point or damage/disable some defensive measure so a heavier and riskier has a better chance of succeeding without leaving the attacker vulnerable to to getting pinned down by their target immediately afterwords. (Mechanically not getting crashed when initiative resets after the decisive.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T05:28:43-07:00","id":1395814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1395619#post1395619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> nor the films of Guillermo del Toro.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think one reasonable point of view is that the Charm names are what a character might call that power, if they happened to identify it as a specific technique. Like the Lunar Charm names use a lot of animal metaphors because Lunars would tend to describe their powers with animal metaphors if called upon to do so, even if Lunars from a particular part of Creation that have never seen that animal wouldn't use that specific one. I think it's reasonable to assume that all the animals mentioned in Lunar Charm titles exist in Creation for this reason.<br /> <br /> Like, one very clear influence on Exalted, and on the Charm names in particular, is martial arts and similar stories where people yell out the name of their technique before doing an attack. I'm very happy that the Exalted developers didn't want to make everyone into this type of character, or let someone who discovered a unique Charm following their personal journey run into someone who says &quot;oh, that's such-and-such technique&quot;. But it seems equally silly to me to say that these types of characters don't exist in exalted, or are limited to specifically yelling out the martial arts charm names, or to forbid people from shouting &quot;Monkey Leap Technique!&quot; when they jump 20 feet into the air. </div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with everything you have written here.<br /> <br /> You absolutely should feel free to shout &quot;Monkey Leap Technique&quot;. You should not feel obligated to do so. Your character might not know what a monkey is. Your character might shout out <a href=\"https://youtu.be/eGASIGiMyi8\" target=\"_blank\">something completely different</a>. They don't have to shout out anything.<br /> <br /> What I am hesitant about is assuming that if a word is used in a Charm name then this denotes that something exists in Creation exactly as it exists on Earth with exactly the same connotations. Especially if it's a word that could have mutliple meanings. <i>Especially</i> if it's a something made from gunpowder.<br /> <br /> Fireworks exist in Creation. But the Charm names are not good evidence of this.<br /> <br /> For Lunar Charms and animals specifically... does a Dodo exist here on Earth? We have an idiom: dead as a Dodo. I think Lunar Charm names are similiar. Something identifiable as the animals mentioned in the Lunar Charms either do exist, did exist, or is recognisable in the mythology of Creation. I think that's reasonable. I think it's unreasonable to draw broad inference from that. &quot;This Lunar Charm says &quot;mammoth&quot; so modern elephants can't have evolved yet&quot; is not a reasonable inference. That &quot;mammoths&quot; exist/existed/are recognisable in (some parts of) Creation is reasonable.<br /> <br /> That the word &quot;firecracker&quot; is used in a Charm name shows that the word probably has meaning in Creation. (It's not &quot;super anachronistic&quot;.) But it's not reasonable to infer that this meaning is exactly the same as on Earth. (Especially as magical ways of making fireworks exist.)<br /> <br /> (That said, I think firecrackers DO exist in Creation. My sole and only point is that the name of the Charm is not good evidence of this.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-11-2020, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T11:23:02-07:00","id":1395865,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the idea that fireworks may be less of the controlled colored explosions in patterns like on earth and might be more like things that send up flame trails into different designs and patterns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T13:05:18-07:00","id":1395895,"title":"","content":"If it hasn't changed in this edition, steam cannon artillery pieces are a thing. So you could have steam-powered launchers. Somebody could probably come up with a water-rocket style pump presure into water. Alternately, imbue the firework with the lightness of elemental air to make them fly up. Or hang them from a kite. Or throw them really hard. Etc Etc<br /> <br /> On the colorful ball of light end, firedust &amp; alchemy could both make sense. <br /> <br /> Or, you could get minions to do all the heavy lifting. &quot;Fire elementals, go do this colorful dance in the air to entertain the Dynast&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T15:17:24-07:00","id":1396077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1395895#post1395895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it hasn't changed in this edition, steam cannon artillery pieces are a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In former editions, <b>steam cannons</b> worked by rapid boiling water using flame dust. Varangian steam cannons have not received any mention in third edition, but <b>fire cannons</b> have been stated up in Arms of the Chosen - including the Lookshy's harbor cannons. Fire cannons are still siege scale flame weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T18:18:51-07:00","id":1396088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1396077#post1396077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In former editions, <b>steam cannons</b> worked by rapid boiling water using flame dust. Varangian steam cannons have not received any mention in third edition, but <b>fire cannons</b> have been stated up in Arms of the Chosen - including the Lookshy's harbor cannons. Fire cannons are still siege scale flame weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e described the shore cannons of Chiaroscuro as steam-powered, but 1e didn't. In 1e, the only steam cannons presumably were from Autochthonia (the crossbow Charm was described as steam powered, at least, so one could imagine that this sort of thing was well-known on the other side of the seal) and didn't work by burning firedust, since they had access to different, typically more potent, sources of heat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T04:16:34-07:00","id":1396150,"title":"","content":"Pyrotechnics overtly utilizing the supernatural is appropriate in spots, I'd find it particularly fitting for the likes of Mahalanka considering descriptions of their industry and the general vibe of &quot;we live beneath the wonders of Raksi&quot;, but not for the setting as a whole. By and large, the world of Exalted during the Age of Sorrows is one in which the magical complements rather than substitutes; a field god might occasionally deign to provide insight into words of encouragement that can be given to seeds as they're sewn, but that won't work without their intervention and for the most part farmers are doing work in familiar and prosaic ways.<br /> <br /> As the Realm goes, the image of their society is not so much built on the direct mystical interventions of the Dragon Blooded as society and capital being able to flourish under their auspices (and ultimately to their benefit). Most people will be familiar with the kinds of fireworks that an otherwise unremarkable craftsperson will put together, because the economy supports such a profession and the culture encourages such a delight as a way of keeping people invested in the idea of the Realm as the best society ever. That keeps them engaged in the kind of work that readily funds the Dragon Blooded doing things like binding salamanders or something into sprucing up <i>their</i> social events (even if a lot of the time it's probably more practical to just also use fireworks of the highest quality and greatest quantity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T04:56:51-07:00","id":1396353,"title":"","content":"Honestly.<br /> <br /> I just wish the books would have a sidebar which acknowledged that firedust possesses similarities to gunpowder and explained the limitation on firearms in thematic terms so people can make an informed decision about their potential inclusion. You can probably get pretty far in before you have to deal with genre clash that gun cultists will try and impose when they roll their eyes at the ridiculousness of people dodging bullets when they were totally fine with people dodging lightning bolts and explosions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:25:27-07:00","id":1396409,"title":"","content":"You know, I find part of the problem with referring to \u201calchemical fireworks\u201d is that the writing doesn\u2019t exactly have a consistent standard for what alchemy refers to. It could be anything from \u201cthis is an instance of the actual transmutation that is possible in this setting\u201d to \u201cthis is basic chemistry, but that term would be a bit anachronistic here\u201d. Without that clarity, the phrase \u201calchemical fireworks\u201d might make about as much sense as referring to chemical cakes; not wrong, but an unnecessary level of detail*.<br /> <br /> Mind, while historically the experimentations of alchemists may have been what led to discoveries of incendiary substances (and the fact that certain salts burn with vivid colours), they would not have been the ones engaging in the work of devising and manufacturing fireworks (which would not have been regarded as alchemy). A work that might have carried a certain prestige, but was still dirty and dangerous and left unpalatable marks even by the standards of pre-modern manufacturing.<br /> <br /> That really goes for most things regarding chemistry throughout history. People have been employing the chemical properties of substances, raw or refined, for various purposes for thousands of years. They just wouldn\u2019t have thought about how those processes worked in the way that we do, and unsophisticated techniques and safety standards tend to relegate them to lower strata of society. Everybody wants dyed cloth, few want to associate or live near the dyers, because their fingers are an unsightly colour and they smell (they\u2019re also possibly giving themselves cancer).<br /> <br /> The people in the setting undertaking the raw work of leaching lye (valuable as a cleaning agent) and potash (used to bleach cloth and make glass or soap) from burnt up wood, do you think of them as alchemists? They probably wouldn\u2019t look the part you imagine attached to that term anyway, they\u2019re working with some caustic shit and I expect there are no rubber gloves.<br /> <br /> Armourers have at least benefitted from the prestige of their craft, but still not quite credited as people on the cutting edge of material science (such as it can be when lacking a unified technical knowledge base) for most of history. There\u2019s a period spanning a few centuries of European history in particular when these were the ones in a constant drive to figure out innovations in the improvement and overcoming of defensive gear. That didn\u2019t just happen on its own, nor was it undertaken by people that we would recognise as scientists. Or alchemists, come to that.<br /> <br /> Which handily leads into another point:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1396353#post1396353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly.<br /> <br /> I just wish the books would have a sidebar which acknowledged that firedust possesses similarities to gunpowder and explained the limitation on firearms in thematic terms so people can make an informed decision about their potential inclusion. You can probably get pretty far in before you have to deal with genre clash that gun cultists will try and impose when they roll their eyes at the ridiculousness of people dodging bullets when they were totally fine with people dodging lightning bolts and explosions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ultimately see no reason to get hung up on justifying the tactical application of incendiaries in the setting, because the setting is already a barely coherent morass of wildly differing equipment types and tactical systems, which just doesn\u2019t make much logical sense. We don\u2019t really get an impression that these are the result of a natural evolution of armies and soldiers constantly attempting to one up each other in pursuit of such things as success in warfare and not dying. To that end, I\u2019d almost ask why <i>not</i> have black powder in the setting? The barest hint of logic can be introduced with the proposition that it does not impress as much in warfare as the more dramatically satisfying \u201cwhoosh\u201d produced when you light firedust, even if it\u2019s a more economic basis for your light shows.<br /> <br /> *I\u2019d want to know if the intent is that fireworks function by transmutation, but I\u2019d also be kind of against that. Notwithstanding the general reservations about introducing transmutation as a function of apparently mundane Craft skill, with no guidance, in the entry for bats of all things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T11:55:35-07:00","id":1396436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1396409#post1396409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ultimately see no reason to get hung up on justifying the tactical application of incendiaries in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but the harbour cannon entry in Arms of the Chosen takes the trouble to explain why firedust can be used propel cannon balls but can't work like that on a smaller scale so at least one of the writers saw fit to address guns in an indirect fashion.<br /> <br /> One of the greatest strengths of Ex3 is that it has actual leadership who can give us clear statements of intent rather than giving a fictional substance particular properties to lead people to a particular conclusion - in this case, that they can't be used to make guns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T15:48:33-07:00","id":1396508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394539-do-fireworks-exsist-in-exalted?p=1394550#post1394550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hope that's some help at least...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is monstrously helpful, Moss Reynholm. Clear answer with a quote. Can't do better.<br /> <br /> Thank you.<br /> __________________________________________________ ______________________________<br /> <br /> Could I ask for you, LadyLens, &amp; habitableexoplanet to consider getting an avatar?<br /> <br /> I am a visual person &amp; I hate confusing proactive &amp; helpful posters due to anon avatar placeholders.<br /> <br /> All of your posts &amp; contributions deserve to stand out.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}